{
  "summary": "The root cause is that the `getKey()` JavaScript function is defined inside `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` conditional blocks in both `client.html` and `index.html`. When a user is already authenticated (key provided via URL), `ShowKeyModal` is false, so the `getKey()` function is never rendered into the page. All edit save functions (description, title, type, done-script) call `getKey()` to pass the auth key as a query parameter, causing an uncaught `ReferenceError: getKey is not defined` when the save button is clicked. The fix is to move the `getKey()` function definition outside the `{{if .ShowKeyModal}}` conditional block so it's always available, or alternatively use the `_dashKey` variable (which is always defined from the Go template `{{.Key}}`) directly in the edit functions instead of calling `getKey()`. The simplest fix would be to replace all `getKey()` calls in edit functions with just using `_dashKey`, which is already the approach used by most other API calls in the same files (e.g., move, restart, auto-mode, scripts)."
}
